From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kuncy7 <noreply@example.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 09:37:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 087/119] net: bridge: keep the default PVID of a new bridge

0966 (QSDK "bridge: Fixes for Bridge VLAN Filtering") disables the
default PVID of every bridge at NETDEV_REGISTER, so each bridge starts
with default_pvid=0 and no VLAN on its ports or on itself. Turning on
vlan_filtering on such a bridge without bridge-vlan sections then drops
every frame in br_allowed_ingress() and the LAN dies. Measured over Wi-Fi
on a GL-B3000: default_pvid=0 and an empty
`bridge vlan show` after boot; `vlan_filtering 1` -> 0/20 pings, with
`vlan_default_pvid 1` set first -> 20/20.

netifd does not need it: with bridge-vlan sections it deletes VLAN 1
from the bridge and from every member itself, and without them it
relies on the kernel default. Keep the kernel default - VLAN 1 PVID
untagged - as upstream does. The rest of 0966 (the bridge VLAN lookups
ECM uses) stays as it is.
---
 net/bridge/br.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/bridge/br.c b/net/bridge/br.c
index c8ccd3c80..a5e5b2db1 100644
--- a/net/bridge/br.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br.c
@@ -47,10 +47,6 @@ static int br_device_event(struct notifier_block *unused, unsigned long event, v
 			return notifier_from_errno(err);
 
 		if (event == NETDEV_REGISTER) {
-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_BRIDGE_VLAN_FILTERING)
-			br_vlan_disable_default_pvid(netdev_priv(dev));
-#endif
-
 			/* register of bridge completed, add sysfs entries */
 			err = br_sysfs_addbr(dev);
 			if (err)
